nteractive storytelling companies"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Internship roles"},{"type":"p","text":"Look for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Script reader"},{"text":"Story intern"},{"text":"Development intern"},{"text":"Creative intern"},{"text":"Research intern"},{"text":"Content intern"},{"text":"Editorial intern"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Internship Portfolio"},{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, aim to have:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"10+ script coverages"},{"text":"5 story breakdowns"},{"text":"3 development memos"},{"text":"2 original screenplays"},{"text":"1 series bible"},{"text":"1 adaptation report"},{"text":"1 industry trend report"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Keep the work organised as a professional portfolio, subject to confidentiality restrictions on scripts provided by employers."}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Priority"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Screenwriting"},{"text":"Story structure"},{"text":"Film analysis"},{"text":"Script development"},{"text":"Creative writing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Additional"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Film production fundamentals"},{"text":"Editing fundamentals"},{"text":"Direction fundamentals"},{"text":"Literary criticism"},{"text":"Audience research"},{"text":"Digital storytelling"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Screenwriting software"},{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Notion"},{"text":"Basic data analysis"},{"text":"AI-assisted research"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Certificates are secondary to strong analytical writing and an excellent story-analysis portfolio."}]},{"heading":"Careers You Can Be Hired As","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Entry level"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Script Reader Intern"},{"text":"Story Intern"},{"text":"Development Intern"},{"text":"Creative Intern"},{"text":"Content Research Intern"},{"text":"Editorial Intern"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Core"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Story Analyst"},{"text":"Script Reader"},{"text":"Script Analyst"},{"text":"Content Analyst"},{"text":"Story Development Associate"},{"text":"Creative Development Associate"},{"text":"Literary Reader"},{"text":"Development Researcher"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Developing"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Senior Story Analyst"},{"text":"Story Editor"},{"text":"Development Executive"},{"text":"Creative Producer"},{"text":"Content Development Executive"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Specialist"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Script Consultant"},{"text":"Story Consultant"},{"text":"Narrative Consultant"},{"text":"Adaptation Consultant"},{"text":"Narrative Designer"},{"text":"Dramaturg"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Leadership"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Creative Development Manager"},{"text":"Head of Development"},{"text":"Creative Executive"},{"text":"Content Development Head"}]},{"type":"h","text":"What Employers May Test"},{"type":"h","text":"Script coverage"},{"type":"p","text":"Read a screenplay and write a one-page professional coverage report."},{"type":"h","text":"Structure"},{"type":"p","text":"Identify the protagonist, central conflict, turning points and climax."},{"type":"h","text":"Character"},{"type":"p","text":"Explain why the protagonist's character arc is or isn't convincing."},{"type":"h","text":"Pacing"},{"type":"p","text":"Identify three sections where the story loses momentum and explain why."},{"type":"h","text":"Development notes"},{"type":"p","text":"Give the writer five actionable improvements without rewriting the entire script."},{"type":"h","text":"Commercial analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"Would this story be better suited to a feature film, limited series, or episodic series?"},{"type":"h","text":"Adaptation"},{"type":"p","text":"Identify what would need to change when adapting a novel into a two-hour film."},{"type":"h","text":"Practical assignment"},{"type":"p","text":"A strong candidate may receive an unpublished script and be asked to produce:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Logline"},{"text":"Synopsis"},{"text":"Genre"},{"text":"Character assessment"},{"text":"Structure assessment"},{"text":"Strengths"},{"text":"Weaknesses"},{"text":"Development notes"},{"text":"Audience assessment"},{"text":"Recommendation"}]}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate Study in India","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Film"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MA Film Studies"},{"text":"MA Film & Television"},{"text":"Film Direction"},{"text":"Screenwriting"},{"text":"Film Production"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Writing"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MA Creative Writing"},{"text":"MFA Creative Writing"},{"text":"Screenwriting"},{"text":"Dramatic Writing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Media"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MA Media Studies"},{"text":"MA Mass Communication"},{"text":"Media & Entertainment"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Specialist"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Film Criticism"},{"text":"Film Theory"},{"text":"Digital Storytelling"},{"text":"Narrative Studies"}]}]},{"heading":"Study Abroad","kind":"abroad","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Potential master's areas:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Screenwriting"},{"text":"Film Studies"},{"text":"Film & Television"},{"text":"Creative Writing"},{"text":"Dramatic Writing"},{"text":"Film Production"},{"text":"Script Development"},{"text":"Storytelling"},{"text":"Narrative Studies"},{"text":"Media & Entertainment"},{"text":"Digital Storytelling"},{"text":"Interactive Media"},{"text":"Game Narrative Design"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Strong combinations"},{"type":"h","text":"Screenwriting + Story Development"},{"type":"h","text":"Film Studies + Film Industry"},{"type":"h","text":"Creative Writing + Screenwriting"},{"type":"h","text":"Film + Digital Storytelling"},{"type":"h","text":"Screenwriting + AI/Narrative Technology"}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Script Reading Intern","Script Reader / Story Analyst","Senior Story Analyst","Story Editor / Development Associate","Development Executive","Creative Development Manager","Head of Development","Creative Executive / Content Head"]},{"type":"h","text":"Independent route"},{"type":"flow","items":["Story Analyst","Script Consultant","Story Consultant","Narrative Consultant","Independent Story Development Specialist"]},{"type":"h","text":"2040–2046 Career Evolution"},{"type":"p","text":"Story analysis will increasingly combine human narrative judgement with AI-assisted screenplay analytics, audience research, content discovery, and interactive storytelling."},{"type":"h","text":"Emerging roles"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI Story Analyst"},{"text":"Narrative Intelligence Analyst"},{"text":"AI-Assisted Script Development Specialist"},{"text":"Story Data Analyst"},{"text":"Interactive Narrative Designer"},{"text":"Virtual Production Story Developer"},{"text":"Transmedia Story Strategist"},{"text":"Digital Narrative Consultant"},{"text":"AI Narrative Evaluation Specialist"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Future workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Screenplay / Story","AI-Assisted Structural Analysis","Character / Theme / Pacing Analysis","Audience & Market Data","Human Story Analyst","Development Notes","Writer / Producer"]},{"type":"p","text":"AI can identify patterns in structure, dialogue, pacing, character presence, and genre conventions, but originality, cultural nuance, emotional resonance, artistic judgement, and creative intent remain difficult to evaluate reliably without human expertise."},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended Final Skill Stack"},{"type":"h","text":"Story"},{"type":"flow","items":["Narrative Structure","Character","Conflict","Theme","Pacing"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Screenwriting"},{"type":"flow","items":["Screenplay Format","Logline","Treatment","Beat Sheet","Series Bible"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Analysis"},{"type":"flow","items":["Script Coverage","Story Diagnostics","Genre Analysis","Audience Analysis"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Film"},{"type":"flow","items":["Film Language","Film History","Direction","Editing","Production"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Industry"},{"type":"flow","items":["Content Development","Production","Streaming","Audience","IP"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Writing"},{"type":"flow","items":["Professional Notes","Development Memos","Critical Writing"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Digital"},{"type":"flow","items":["Screenwriting Software","Research Tools","Basic Data Analytics"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Emerging"},{"type":"flow","items":["AI-Assisted Story Analysis","Narrative Analytics","Interactive Storytelling"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Target Progression"},{"type":"h","text":"0–2 years"},{"type":"flow","items":["Script Reader Intern","Script Reader","Story Analyst"]},{"type":"h","text":"2–5 years"},{"type":"flow","items":["Story Analyst","Senior Story Analyst","Development Associate"]},{"type":"h","text":"5–8 years"},{"type":"flow","items":["Story Editor","Development Executive","Creative Development Manager"]},{"type":"h","text":"8+ years"},{"type":"flow","items":["Head of Development","Creative Executive","Story/Content Consultant"]},{"type":"h","text":"Best overall strategy"},{"type":"p","text":"For BA Creative Writing / Film Studies / Screenwriting → Story Analyst, build:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Screenwriting","Film Analysis","Script Coverage","Narrative Theory","Industry Knowledge","Professional Writing"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"The most important asset is a high-quality story-analysis portfolio. By graduation, the student should be able to read an unfamiliar screenplay and quickly identify its premise, structure, character arcs, pacing, thematic strengths, weaknesses, audience positioning, and development opportunities."},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest long-term profile combines creative judgement with industry awareness and data/AI literacy, allowing progression from traditional script reading into story development, content strategy, narrative consulting, and AI-assisted creative development."}]}]}